IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ea89-types`
IMPORT `ea89-days`

-- Electricity Act 1989 (UK) — GOAL 1: CONNECTION (ss 16-23).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1989-29.txt.
-- The customer asks: "Must the distributor connect my premises, or keep them
-- connected; when can it disconnect me; what interest is due on my security;
-- and until when can I refer a dispute to Ofgem?"

§ `Goal 1 — connection`

-- s 16A(1)-(2): a notice requiring terms, specifying the premises, the date
-- and the maximum power.
@ref s 16A(1)-(2)
GIVEN r IS A `Connection request`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a valid notice has been given for` r IF
    CONSIDER r's `notice given on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST n  THEN r's `the notice specifies premises, date and maximum power`

-- s 17(1)(a), (b), (ba) and (2): the distributor need not connect (or
-- maintain), without any notice.
@ref s 17(1)(a)-(ba), (2)
GIVEN r IS A `Connection request`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 17 excludes without notice` r IF
        r's `the distributor is prevented by circumstances outside its control`
    OR  r's `a breach of safety regulations despite reasonable steps`
    OR  r's `not in accordance with the designated strategic plans`
    OR  r's `a Schedule 3 or 4 power is needed without consent`

@ref ss 16(1), (4), 16A, 17, 20(1A), 22(2)
@export Must the electricity distributor connect my premises, or maintain my connection, under ss 16-22 of the Electricity Act 1989 (UK)? The duty arises when the owner or occupier (or a supplier with their consent) gives a notice under s 16A specifying the premises, the date and the maximum power; it gives way to a special connection agreement (s 22), to the exceptions in s 17(1)-(2) (for an existing connection, s 17(1)(c) allows disconnection only after 7 working days' notice: see the disconnection goal), and to a failure to give security (s 20(1A)). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN r IS A `Connection request`  @desc Who requires the connection, any special agreement, whether connected already, the notice, and the distributor's circumstances
GIVETH A `Connection outcome`
`must the distributor connect` r MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF r's `a special connection agreement is effective`  THEN `the special connection agreement governs`
        IF r's `already connected`                            THEN
            BRANCH
                IF `s 17 excludes without notice` r            THEN `need not connect under s 17`
                IF r's `security required and not given`       THEN `may disconnect for want of security`
                OTHERWISE                                           `must maintain the connection`
        IF NOT (r's `required by the owner or occupier, or a supplier with consent`)
                                                              THEN `the duty is not engaged`
        IF NOT (`a valid notice has been given for` r)         THEN `no valid notice yet`
        IF `s 17 excludes without notice` r
            OR r's `not reasonable in all the circumstances`  THEN `need not connect under s 17`
        IF r's `security required and not given`              THEN `may refuse the lines or plant until security is given`
        OTHERWISE                                                  `must offer terms and connect`

-- s 17(3): s 17(1)(c) "does not permit an electricity distributor to
-- disconnect any premises ... to which a connection is being maintained by
-- him unless the distributor gives ... not less than seven working days'
-- notice of his intention to disconnect". The earliest day is the seventh
-- working day after the day of the notice (F2).
@ref s 17(1)(c), (3)
@export The earliest day the electricity distributor may disconnect my maintained connection on the ground that it is not reasonable to require it (s 17(1)(c) and (3) of the Electricity Act 1989 (UK)): the seventh working day after the day it gave me notice of its intention. NOTHING if the connection is not maintained, the ground does not apply, or no notice was given. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN r IS A `Connection request`         @desc The connection, the s 17(1)(c) finding, and the disconnection notice
      holidays IS A LIST OF DATE           @desc The bank holidays
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the earliest day I can be disconnected under s 17(1)(c) for` r `, bank holidays` holidays MEANS
    IF     NOT (r's `already connected`)
        OR NOT (r's `not reasonable in all the circumstances`)
        OR r's `a special connection agreement is effective`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE
        CONSIDER r's `disconnection notice given on`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST n  THEN JUST (`the` 7 `th working day after` n `, bank holidays` holidays)

@ref s 17(1)(c), (3)
GIVEN r IS A `Connection request`, holidays IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disconnection under s 17(1)(c) is allowed on the day for` r `, bank holidays` holidays IF
    CONSIDER `the earliest day I can be disconnected under s 17(1)(c) for` r `, bank holidays` holidays
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST e  THEN
        CONSIDER r's `disconnection on`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST d  THEN d AT LEAST e

-- s 20(3): interest "on every sum of 50p so deposited for every three months
-- during which it remains in the hands of the distributor". Only whole sums
-- of 50p and whole periods of three months count (F3).
@ref s 20(3)
@export The interest the distributor must pay on money I deposited as security under s 20(3) of the Electricity Act 1989 (UK): the rate it fixed, for every whole 50p deposited, for every whole three months the money stays with it. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN s IS A `Security deposit`  @desc The amount deposited, the rate per 50p per three months, and the days it was deposited and returned
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the interest on my security deposit` s MEANS
    fifties TIMES quarters TIMES s's `interest per 50p per three months`
    WHERE
        fifties MEANS FLOOR (2 TIMES s's `amount deposited`)
        quarters MEANS `whole three-month periods from` (s's `deposited on`) `to` (s's `returned on`) `counted` 0

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE, k IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`whole three-month periods from` a `to` b `counted` k MEANS
    IF `add months` a (3 TIMES (k PLUS 1)) AT MOST b
    THEN `whole three-month periods from` a `to` b `counted` (k PLUS 1)
    ELSE k

-- s 23(1C): "No dispute ... which relates to the making of a connection ...
-- may be referred to the Authority after the end of the period of 12 months
-- beginning with the time when the connection is made." The last day is the
-- day before the corresponding date (F4).
@ref s 23(1C)
@export The last day I can refer a dispute about the making of my connection to Ofgem (the Authority) under s 23(1C) of the Electricity Act 1989 (UK): the end of the 12 months beginning with the day the connection was made. NOTHING if the connection has not been made. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN r IS A `Connection request`  @desc The day the connection was made
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day to refer a connection dispute for` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r's `connection made on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST c  THEN
        IF   DATE_DAY (`add months` c 12) EQUALS DATE_DAY c
        THEN JUST (`the day before` (`add months` c 12))
        ELSE JUST (`add months` c 12)
